      "subject": "הקשית לשאול",
      "rationale": "Literally 'you have made-hard to ask' — idiom for 'you have asked a hard thing'; the literal kept here exposes the hiphil causative."
    },
    {
      "kind": "addition",
      "subject": "the asking",
      "rationale": "English needs a noun object for the infinitive לשאול; the Hebrew has only the bare infinitive."
    },
    {
      "kind": "mystery",
      "subject": "Elijah's answer",
      "rationale": "The condition is left unstated by whom it is controlled — the taking is seen, not caused, and the grant is conditional on a sign not a deed."
    }
  ],
